{"abstract":[{"text":"Distinguishes multiple octave shifts occurring simultaneously.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"metadata":{"title":"number","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLOctaveShiftV6numberAA14MXLNumberLevelVSgvp","symbolKind":"property","roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"number"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNumberLevelV","text":"MXLNumberLevel"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOctaveShift"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxloctaveshift\/number"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"number"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNumberLevelV","text":"MXLNumberLevel"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to the MusicXML "},{"code":"number","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" attribute."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOctaveShift\/number"},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLOctaveShift":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLOctaveShift","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOctaveShift","title":"MXLOctaveShift","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The octave shift type indicates where notes are shifted up or down from their true pitched values because of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"printing difficulty. Thus a treble clef line noted with 8va will be indicated with an octave-shift down from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the pitch data indicated in the notes. A size of 8 indicates one octave; a size of 15 indicates two octaves."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLOctaveShift","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxloctaveshift"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNumberLevel":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumberlevel","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNumberLevel","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Slurs, tuplets, and many other features can be concurrent and overlap within a single musical part. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"number-level entity distinguishes up to 16 concurrent objects of the same type when the objects overlap in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"MusicXML document order. Values greater than 6 are usually only needed for music with a large number of divisi"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"staves in a single part, or if there are more than 6 cross-staff arpeggios in a single measure. When a number-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"level value is implied, the value is 1 by default."}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLNumberLevel","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLNumberLevel"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLOctaveShift/number":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"number","abstract":[{"text":"Distinguishes multiple octave shifts occurring simultaneously.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOctaveShift\/number","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"number"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNumberLevelV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLNumberLevel"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxloctaveshift\/number"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"}}}